{"overclaims":[{"abstract":"The quantitative and qualitative results showed that prospective teachers in the experimental group significantly and positively impacted TPACK and its seven domains.","body":"the use of DVRs had a significant impact on all TPACK domains except for technological knowledge (TK)","body_loc":"","cell_sentence_id":"results.2","why":"The quote states the impact was significant on all domains except TK, which is narrower than the claim of a significant impact on all seven domains."},{"abstract":"Analyzing digital video recordings (DVRs) is an effective instructional strategy for professionally preparing and developing prospective teachers.","body":"The generalization of the results should take into account the fact that the responses are self-reported.","body_loc":"","cell_sentence_id":"discussion.4","why":"The effectiveness claim rests on self-reported questionnaire responses, and the body asks that generalization of the results take this into account."},{"abstract":"Therefore, the results of the current study provide concrete evidence for the need to use DVRs as a promising educational approach in future professional preparation and to develop prospective teachers’ technological pedagogical content knowledge (TPACK).","body":"The main limitation was the inability to provide a unified control group and a unified experimental group, especially since practical training groups are small groups.","body_loc":"","cell_sentence_id":"discussion.4","why":"The 'concrete evidence' claim is weakened by the stated limitation that the control and experimental groups could not be unified."}],"unsettled":["The results of the study indicated that digital video recordings allowed prospective teachers to reflect and ponder on their teaching skills, content delivery, and the appropriate use of technology and its relevant tools in the educational process to identify strengths for development and weaknesses for improvement."]}